==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 50% HP:
**1 [[The Face]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 2.67~6 seconds<sup>80f~180f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn, delay 2.67~6 seconds<sup>80f~180f</sup>.
**1 [[Mooth]] spawns.
**1 [[Mooth]] spawns.
**1 [[Shy Boy]] spawns.
**1 [[Shy Boy]] spawns.

==Strategy==
This stage features The Face and Shy Boys together, which makes for a particularly nasty combo. Fortunately, the Shy Boys are much faster than their support, so it is possible to lure them away and pick them off. To do so, create a large gap in your defenses to allow the Shy Boys to move ahead unimpeded. Once they are successfully lured away, spam your meatshields and attackers to quickly take them out. With the Shy Boys down, just clean up the Face in the back and you win.

Additionally, you can stall the weak Doges at the start of the level for money. Once you have accumulated plenty of cash, begin to push toward the base. [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|Anti-Red]] units such as [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Whale Cat]] and [[Axe Cat (Normal Cat)|Brave Cat]] are especially effective against the Shy Boys. Units with high range, such as [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]] and [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]], can safely defeat the enemies with their range advantage. If you have them, gacha units like [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Ring Girl Cat]] and [[Bath Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bath Cat]] are very good here.

